{{Historical content|As of [[Version 3.23.0]], [[the Labyrinth]] no longer provides Labyrinth enchantments as rewards. The [[Divine Font]] now rewards [[transfigured gem]]s and gem-related rewards instead. Labyrinth enchantments can only be found on already-enchanted items in [[permanent leagues]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3452002#5|title=Path of Exile 2 and Path of Exile: Affliction Recently Asked Questions|date=December 3, 2023|accessdate=December 3, 2023}}</ref>}}
'''Labyrinth enchantments''' are a type of [[enchantment]] that used to be obtained from [[the Labyrinth]]. Completing the Labyrinth and interacting with the [[Divine Font]] in the final room would allow a piece of equipment to be imbued with a random enchantment. The eligible equipment types and the tier of the enchantment depended on the difficulty of the Labyrinth challenge. Each party member gained a use of the Divine Font upon completion of a lab if completed by a party. 

* Normal Lab: Gloves (T1)
* Cruel Lab: Gloves (T2), Boots (T1) 
* Merciless Lab: Gloves (T3), Boots (T2), Helmets (T1)
* Eternal (Uber) Lab or [[The_Lord's_Labyrinth#Enriched_Eternal_Labyrinth|Enriched Lab]]: Gloves (T4), Boots (T3), Helmets (T2)
* Enriched Lab using {{il|Dedication to the Goddess}}: Gloves (T4), Boots (T3), Helmets (T2), Belts (T1) 

==Glove enchantments==
{{main|List of glove enchantment mods}}
[[Gloves]] can have enchantments with effects that trigger a Word skill during combat. Word skills cannot be modified by support gems, and have a short cooldown between activation. Glove enchantments come in four tiers, based on difficulty: ''Words'' for normal, ''Edicts'' for cruel, ''Decrees'' for merciless, and ''Commandment'' for eternal. Higher difficulties result in stronger Word skills.

{{#lst:List of glove enchantment mods}}

==Boot enchantments==
{{main|List of boot enchantment mods}}
[[Boots]] can have enchantments with effects that conditionally benefit the player in combat, such as triggering when [[hit]] or not having taken damage [[recently]].

The total weight of all possible enchantments is 1450,{{citation needed}} resulting in an effective encounter rate of 6.9% for mods weighted 100, and 1.72% for mods weighted 25.

{{#lst:List of boot enchantment mods}}

==Helmet enchantments==
{{main|List of helmet enchantment mods}}
[[Helmets]] can have enchantments with effects that affect a specific [[skill]] gem. There are approximately two or three of these skill-specific stats for every skill, amounting to {{Modifier table/count
|q_tables = mod_spawn_weights
|q_join = mods._pageID=mod_spawn_weights._pageID
|q_where = mods.generation_type = 10 AND mod_spawn_weights.tag = "helmet" AND mod_spawn_weights.value > 0
}} in total. ({{Modifier table/count
|q_tables = mod_spawn_weights
|q_join = mods._pageID=mod_spawn_weights._pageID
|q_where = mods.generation_type = 10 AND mod_spawn_weights.tag = "helmet" AND mod_spawn_weights.value > 0 AND mods.required_level = "66"
}} for merc lab and {{Modifier table/count
|q_tables = mod_spawn_weights
|q_join = mods._pageID=mod_spawn_weights._pageID
|q_where = mods.generation_type = 10 AND mod_spawn_weights.tag = "helmet" AND mod_spawn_weights.value > 0 AND mods.required_level = "75"
}} for uber lab versions) The [[Vaal skill|Vaal version]] of a specific skill is also affected by the enchantment of the base skill.<ref name="Enchantments" />

As of [[version 3.22.0]], there were 696 uber lab helmet enchantments. Items that permitted multiple enchantments (e.g. {{il|Cowl of the Cryophile}}) could not roll enchantments for the same skill on a single item.

{{#lst:List of helmet enchantment mods}}

==Belt enchantments==
{{main|List of belt enchantment mods}}
[[Belts]] can have enchantments with conditional effects based around a specific [[buff]] or [[debuff]], such as [[blind]], [[Arcane Surge]], and [[consecrated ground]].

{{#lst:List of belt enchantment mods}}

